Site Report: Market-road, Bori Metropolis.

The interpreted subsurface model for this station consists of five layers. Resistivity increases from 104 ohm-m in the first layer (2.86 m) through 186 ohm-m, 266 ohm-m, and reaches a maximum of 327 ohm-m at the fourth layer (base depth 54.6 m). The sequence concludes with a fifth layer showing a decrease in resistivity to 219 ohm-m. Consequently, the correct curve type for this profile is AAK. Please note that the current on-file classification of AAA-type is inaccurate, as it fails to account for the resistivity reduction in the final layer.

